// OT -- ownership transfer of x through the write to y, release-acquire.
//
// Source: Arlt & Vafeiadis, "RGSep under Release/Acquire Consistency",
//         PACMPL 10 (OOPSLA2), Article 375, 2026. doi:10.1145/3839507, Section 5.2, Fig. 4.
//
// Thread 1 writes x twice while x is local to it, then publishes it with
// y := 1. Thread 2 reads y; if it is non-zero, x must hold 0, otherwise it
// writes y itself. The paper proves assert(c = 0) under RA. c is 0 unless
// thread 2 took the first branch.
//
// Reference verdicts:
//   the paper: under RA, reading y != 0 implies x = 0.
//   herd7 7.58 on herd/OT.litmus, under the zoo's abstract-sc, abstract-tso,
//     ra, sra, wra and abstract-coherence cat models and herd's rc11.cat:
//     Coherence allows; SC, TSO, RA, SRA, WRA and RC11 forbid.
// The paper's registers are renamed b -> rb, c -> rc:
// MoRDor reads only names beginning with r as registers.
x := 0; y := 0;
{ x.store(5, rel); x.store(0, rel); y.store(1, rel) }
||| {
  rb := y.load(acq);
  rc := 0;
  if (rb != 0) { rc := x.load(acq) } else { y.store(1, rel) }
}
%%
allow (rb != 0 && rc != 0) [Coherence]
forbid (rb != 0 && rc != 0) [SC, TSO, RA, SRA, WRA, RC11]
